{%- comment -%}
  Three-panel banner: full-bleed image, a text panel (logo mark, two-line heading, body
  copy, link, and a small product shot), full-bleed image. Built for a triptych layout
  no existing section covers -- collection-list/media-grid only pair one image with one
  text block, never a text-only center panel flanked by two independent images.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if section.settings.left_image != blank or section.settings.right_image != blank or section.settings.heading_line_1 != blank or section.settings.heading_line_2 != blank -%}
  <style>
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
      --triptych-banner-center-background: {{ section.settings.center_background_color.rgb }};
      --triptych-banner-center-text-color: {{ section.settings.color_scheme.settings.text_color.rgb }};
      --triptych-banner-accent-color: {{ section.settings.accent_color.rgb }};
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__media {
      position: relative;
      aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
      Absolutely positioning the photo (rather than a plain width/height: 100%) takes it
      out of normal flow, so its own intrinsic aspect ratio can no longer inflate the
      grid row's `auto` track size -- without this, a tall source photo was winning the
      "auto" side of minmax(desktop_height, auto) and stretching the whole row far past
      the height set in the theme editor, even though the center panel's real content
      needed nowhere near that much room.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__media img,
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__media .placeholder {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      object-fit: cover;
      display: block;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
      These photos are isolated cutouts (transparent background around the subject),
      not full-bleed rectangular shots -- object-fit: cover alone can't crop that empty
      margin away since the subject doesn't fill the source image's own frame. Scaling
      the image up within its (overflow: hidden) box crops the transparent edges out of
      view instead, so only the product/model shows.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__media--left img {
      transform: scale({{ section.settings.left_image_zoom | divided_by: 100.0 }});
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__media--right img {
      transform: scale({{ section.settings.right_image_zoom | divided_by: 100.0 }});
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__content {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      text-align: center;
      gap: 1.25rem;
      padding: 4rem 1.5rem;
      background: rgb(var(--triptych-banner-center-background));
      color: rgb(var(--triptych-banner-center-text-color));
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__logo {
      width: {{ section.settings.logo_width }}px;
      height: auto;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__rule {
      width: 32px;
      height: 1px;
      background: currentColor;
      opacity: .4;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__kicker {
      color: rgb(var(--triptych-banner-center-text-color));
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__heading {
      color: rgb(var(--triptych-banner-accent-color));
    }

    {%- comment -%}
      All three heading lines (kicker + two heading lines) share the same font size --
      they're separate <p> elements only so each can be forced onto its own line and
      colored independently. Tightening the gap between them here makes them read as
      one heading block instead of three separately-spaced paragraphs.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} :is(.triptych-banner__kicker, .triptych-banner__heading) + :is(.triptych-banner__kicker, .triptych-banner__heading) {
      margin-block-start: -.5rem;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__body {
      max-width: 30ch;
    }

    {%- comment -%}
      max-height bounds this alongside max-width: the source photo is a closed
      loop/oval shape (roughly square, not a thin flat strand), so scaling purely by
      width also scales height nearly 1:1 -- a wide product_image_width alone can make
      the shot dominate the panel and shove the button/heading apart. Capping height
      keeps the shot compact regardless of how wide the setting goes.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      transform: scale (rather than a bigger box) so the enlargement is purely visual
      -- a scaled element still reserves its original, unscaled box in the flex layout,
      so growing the shot this way can never push the section taller. It paints outside
      its own box instead of inside it, which is fine here since nothing in this panel
      clips overflow.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__product-image {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: {{ section.settings.product_image_width }}px;
      max-height: 230px;
      height: auto;
      object-fit: contain;
      margin-block-start: .5rem;
      transform: scale(1.4);
    }

    @media screen and (min-width: 1000px) {
      {%- comment -%}
        minmax(desktop_height, auto): desktop_height is a floor, not a hard cap. A hard
        `{{ section.settings.desktop_height }}vh` row plus overflow: hidden was tried
        here and it clipped the logo/kicker/first heading line clean off the top of the
        panel on ordinary laptop-height screens -- the stacked content (logo, 3 heading
        lines, body copy, button, product shot) simply doesn't fit a 50vh-tall panel at
        normal type sizes, so something has to give. Between "sometimes a bit taller
        than desktop_height" and "silently deletes part of the heading", auto is the one
        that never hides content. The tightened sizes below are what keep the *typical*
        case close to desktop_height; auto is the backstop for when it still isn't
        enough room.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;
        grid-template-rows: minmax({{ section.settings.desktop_height }}vh, auto);
      }

      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__media {
        aspect-ratio: auto;
        height: 100%;
      }

      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__content {
        gap: .5rem;
        padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
      }

      {%- comment -%}
        Fixed, meaningfully smaller sizes (not the theme's normal .h1/.h6/logo_width) --
        this panel is a third of a short banner, not a page heading, so it reads at its
        own compact scale regardless of viewport height.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__logo {
        width: min({{ section.settings.logo_width }}px, 40px);
      }

      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} :is(.triptych-banner__kicker, .triptych-banner__heading) {
        font-size: 1.375rem;
        line-height: 1.15;
      }

      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__body {
        font-size: .8rem;
        line-height: 1.4;
      }

      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__content .h6 {
        font-size: .7rem;
      }

      {%- comment -%}
        No max-height cap here (unlike an earlier version of this rule) -- a fixed
        height ceiling silently overrode the product_image_width setting whenever the
        photo's aspect ratio made height the binding constraint under object-fit:
        contain, so the width slider had no visible effect. Width alone is enough: the
        grid row already grows past desktop_height via minmax(..., auto) if the taller
        shot needs more room.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .triptych-banner__product-image {
        width: auto;
        height: auto;
        max-width: min(100%, {{ section.settings.product_image_width }}px);
        object-fit: contain;
        margin-block-start: 0;
        transform: scale(1.4);
      }
    }
  </style>

  <div class="color-scheme color-scheme--{{ section.settings.color_scheme.id }} {% if section.settings.separate_section_with_border %}bordered-section{% endif %}">
    <div class="triptych-banner">
      {%- comment -%}Left image{%- endcomment -%}
      {%- capture left_media -%}
        {%- if section.settings.left_image != blank -%}
          {{- section.settings.left_image | image_url: width: section.settings.left_image.width | image_tag: sizes: '(max-width: 999px) 100vw, 33vw', widths: '400,600,800,1000,1200,1600', loading: 'lazy', alt: section.settings.left_image_alt | default: '' -}}
        {%- else -%}
          {{- 'lifestyle-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder' -}}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- if section.settings.left_image_link != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ section.settings.left_image_link }}" class="triptych-banner__media triptych-banner__media--left">{{- left_media -}}</a>
      {%- else -%}
        <div class="triptych-banner__media triptych-banner__media--left">{{- left_media -}}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}Center content{%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="triptych-banner__content">
        {%- if section.settings.logo_image != blank -%}
          {{- section.settings.logo_image | image_url: width: 160 | image_tag: widths: '80,160', alt: '', loading: 'lazy', class: 'triptych-banner__logo' -}}
        {%- endif -%}

        <span class="triptych-banner__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>

        <div class="prose">
          {%- if section.settings.kicker_text != blank -%}
            <p class="triptych-banner__kicker h1">{{- section.settings.kicker_text -}}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.heading_line_1 != blank -%}
            <p class="triptych-banner__heading h1">{{- section.settings.heading_line_1 -}}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.heading_line_2 != blank -%}
            <p class="triptych-banner__heading h1">{{- section.settings.heading_line_2 -}}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.body_text != blank -%}
            <div class="triptych-banner__body">{{- section.settings.body_text -}}</div>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.button_text != blank -%}
            <p class="h6">
              {%- render 'button', href: section.settings.button_link, content: section.settings.button_text, style: 'link', focusable: false -%}
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- if section.settings.product_image != blank -%}
          {{- section.settings.product_image | image_url: width: section.settings.product_image.width | image_tag: widths: '300,400,600,800', loading: 'lazy', class: 'triptych-banner__product-image', alt: section.settings.product_image_alt | default: '' -}}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}Right image{%- endcomment -%}
      {%- capture right_media -%}
        {%- if section.settings.right_image != blank -%}
          {{- section.settings.right_image | image_url: width: section.settings.right_image.width | image_tag: sizes: '(max-width: 999px) 100vw, 33vw', widths: '400,600,800,1000,1200,1600', loading: 'lazy', alt: section.settings.right_image_alt | default: '' -}}
        {%- else -%}
          {{- 'lifestyle-2' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder' -}}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- if section.settings.right_image_link != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ section.settings.right_image_link }}" class="triptych-banner__media triptych-banner__media--right">{{- right_media -}}</a>
      {%- else -%}
        <div class="triptych-banner__media triptych-banner__media--right">{{- right_media -}}</div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Image / Text / Image",
  "class": "shopify-section--image-text-image-banner",
  "tag": "section",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "custom.overlay"]
  },
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:global.colors.scheme",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "separate_section_with_border",
      "label": "t:global.section.separate_section_with_border",
      "default": false
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "desktop_height",
      "min": 30,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "vh",
      "label": "Desktop height",
      "default": 60
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "accent_color",
      "label": "Heading accent color",
      "default": "#b08d57"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Left image"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "left_image",
      "label": "t:global.image.image"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "left_image_alt",
      "label": "t:global.image.alt_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "left_image_link",
      "label": "t:global.text.link"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "left_image_zoom",
      "min": 100,
      "max": 250,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "label": "Zoom",
      "info": "Crops in on the photo. Useful for cutout/isolated images with empty space around the subject.",
      "default": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Right image"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "right_image",
      "label": "t:global.image.image"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "right_image_alt",
      "label": "t:global.image.alt_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "right_image_link",
      "label": "t:global.text.link"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "right_image_zoom",
      "min": 100,
      "max": 250,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "label": "Zoom",
      "info": "Crops in on the photo. Useful for cutout/isolated images with empty space around the subject.",
      "default": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Center content"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "center_background_color",
      "label": "Background color",
      "default": "#f5f0e6"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "logo_image",
      "label": "Logo mark",
      "info": "Small mark shown above the heading. Falls back to nothing when empty."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "logo_width",
      "min": 20,
      "max": 120,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Logo mark width",
      "default": 48
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "kicker_text",
      "label": "Kicker line",
      "default": "Timeless"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading_line_1",
      "label": "Heading, line 1",
      "default": "Diamond"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading_line_2",
      "label": "Heading, line 2",
      "default": "Essentials"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body_text",
      "label": "t:global.text.content",
      "default": "<p>Modern chains and diamond bracelets, meticulously crafted to elevate every moment, every day.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "button_text",
      "label": "t:global.text.button_text",
      "default": "Shop the Collection"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "button_link",
      "label": "t:global.text.button_link"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "product_image",
      "label": "Product shot",
      "info": "Small image shown below the button, e.g. an isolated product photo."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "product_image_alt",
      "label": "t:global.image.alt_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "product_image_width",
      "min": 120,
      "max": 400,
      "step": 10,
      "unit": "px",
      "label": "Product shot width",
      "default": 260
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Image / Text / Image",
      "category": "t:global.categories.storytelling"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
